mantle rm226
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_ulla_greymore
title the corner turned in
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk turns_marked_corners_in_and_counts_bells_against_a_wrist
likes oatcakes long_walks tidy_house first_snow
dislikes gulls early_bells
fears sending_private_marks_round_the_street
hopes to_give_each_bundle_back_whole
topics work +0.6 home +0.3 travel +0.3 friends +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=careful refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# turns marked corners inside a bundle, counts bell strokes against the wrist, and bristles at questions about other households.

words
oath! = Boil my good cuff | Wrinkle my working thumb
saying! = Return the bundle whole | Turn the private corner in
cornerbit = a marked corner | a corner with black stitching
foldbit = a loose fold | a deep inward tuck
wringbit = a thick twist of linen | a wet roll of cloth
soapend = a cloudy soap heel | a shaving of amber soap
pairstick = a split tally | one half of a notched stick
pinbit = a plain wooden pin | a square peg
walkbit = a long flat stretch | a level road
oatpiece = a broken oatcake | a toasted oat round
whitedust = a drift of clean flakes | a handful of first snow
birdbit = a shriek from a gull | the scrape of a gull's cry
bellbit = a stroke of chapel bronze | a low swinging note
toepatch = an oval patch | a grey patch of cloth
handspan = a paw's breadth | the length of one thumb
stringbit = a thick loop of twine | a bit of soft cord
steambit = a little hot cloud | a fog of kettle steam
threadbit = a short blue thread | a length of black wool
breadrag = a little bread cloth | a clean square for oatcakes

grown

opinion houses against 2 : A grand badge doesn't make the water any lighter for the wolf who lifts it.
opinion dole for 3 : Let the one who brings the bowl choose how full. Hunger has a voice worth hearing.
opinion strangers for 1 : If I've got an oatcake I can find a way to break it cleanly in two.
opinion merchants against 1 : That last bit of soap costs most to the household with the fewest clothes.
opinion festivals against 1 : I'd like room to cross a street on weary legs without shouting setting me spinning.
opinion church for 1 : A chapel bell reaches through the steam when I can't see my own boots.
opinion sump for 1 : I like neighbours who'll give you a hand with a soaking bundle and keep their eyes off the mark.
opinion watch against 1 : Anyone asking to inspect somebody else's business ought to give a reason out loud.
opinion city mixed 1 : There's a hard climb between a rich wolf's doorstep and the hands that keep the linen clean.
line greet : Set down whatever you're carrying. My ears work better when nobody's straining.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : No ceremony needed. You have my attention.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I'll take my first words a little softer.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm listening above my wrists, anyhow.
line greet.return : I've put the sharp edge of my voice away.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : For you I can loosen a little of the day.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk] : A welcome voice to hear with the light going.
line again.open : You caught me before the next bundle of business.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Nearer, if you've got time to stop properly!
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Take an easy hold of my arm. There's room.
line farewell : Leave yourself a bit of unclaimed daylight.
line farewell.return : Go with light hands if you've any say in it.
line react.news : Give me the whole bundle before I judge the weight.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh bit of cloth on the pile.
line react.news.known : I've handled that piece of news once already.
line react.news.doubt : A mark on one corner proves less than you might suppose.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd do a quiet turn of work for whoever's hurting.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|succession|apprentice] : That's worth an extra oatcake and a generous scrape of butter.
line answer.how : My wrists are speaking and I'm letting them finish.
line ask.how : Is anything pulling harder on you than it ought?
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy down to the knuckles. I can still hear you.
line sympathise : Give me one small thing to take off your hands.
line reassure : It needn't all be wrung out in one turn.
line thank : My arms owe you for the weight you've spared.
line deflect_thanks : Doing the little part was easier than standing watching.
line decline : I'd be spending somebody else's trust if I did that.
line accept_decline : I'll take my hands off the matter.
line preclose : I need to let my feet get moving again.
line accept_preclose : Away with you before another job finds you.
line ack : I've got both corners of your meaning now.
line offer : Here, take this corner. It's the driest.
line give.advice : Loosen the knot while you can still get a nail under it.
scene at_self_workplace_i
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I want each bundle back with its owner and its business inside. | If I'm at my work, #self.trade_words#, I turn marks where no idle eye can read them.
b : Wouldn't it be quicker to leave them showing?
a : Quicker for me. Dearer for the one who's got patched clothes on the line. | I don't count time saved by passing somebody's worries round the room.

scene i_turn_a_stitched
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a stitched name inward before I put a bundle down. | A corner can give the game away while a grand front door keeps up appearances.
b : Where does that knowledge belong?
a : Tie it inside. A decent knot can keep a good deal quiet. | Leave it where it came from. My fingers have their own work.

scene butter_ought_to_find
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Butter ought to find the hollows in an oatcake before your teeth do. | If there's a broken oatcake I'll take the piece with the burnt rim.
b : What's good about the edge?
a : A dark edge and a little soft butter give each other something to do. | The crunch gets louder and then all at once it stops. That's a fine mouthful.

scene a_proper_walk_has
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A proper walk has no parcel pulling on either arm. | I like to go out with no load but my coat.
b : Where do you aim for?
a : The place where I stop thinking about what time I ought to turn back. | No particular doorway. That's why the walk feels longer than an errand.

scene i_count_the_chapel
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the chapel bells with my thumb against my wrist. | I lose count if I stop to say the numbers out loud.
b : Does every stroke need counting?
a : No, but I enjoy finding how far my own thoughts have taken me. | The early ones can count themselves without any help from me. They spoil a lovely sleep.

scene the_first_snow_is
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first snow is my favourite coverlet. Nobody has to haul it up the hill. | I'd get out of bed to see the season's first flakes.
b : Even before the bells?
a : For snow, yes. A bell has never made the whole street clean in one breath. | I'd be cross about the hour and delighted at the sight. I can manage both.

scene a_gull_knows_precisely
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull knows precisely when to begin shouting over something worth hearing. | I wouldn't trust a gull alone with an uncovered oatcake.
b : What would you trust it with?
a : The dirty end of a very long line, well clear of everybody else's supper. | Flying its own wings and making its own awful racket.

scene i_want_a_clear
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a clear seat more than a shining shelf. | A tidy room is one I can go into tired without thinking where to put my feet.
b : Where do things go first?
a : Everything sharp goes up high. Everything heavy goes where I won't have to lift it twice. | Leave a clear space inside the threshold for my next armful.

scene i_might_make_a
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I might make a private note of a doubtful mark. I won't read it out for sport. | You can keep an eye on whose coin goes where without calling the street to witness.
b : What if you're pressed for names?
a : I'd press right back for evidence and wait to hear who still wanted to talk. | I'd close the book. Ink shouldn't get a wolf condemned for a guess.

scene a_friend_doesn_t
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend doesn't have to offer both arms when one will do. | I'd rather ask for one definite kindness than leave a friend guessing.
b : What sort of kindness?
a : Hold the door while my elbows are full. It's an ordinary kind of miracle. | Walk a few minutes with me. Leave the day's accounts to settle by themselves.

scene when_i_show_another
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I show another pair of hands a job, I do it once at half speed. | I like a learner to find a grip without my fingers laid over the top.
b : What if the grip's wrong?
a : Stop before anybody gets hurt. Show where the strain goes and start again. | Ask what hurts. There's generally a wrist somewhere answering before the mouth does.

scene my_wrists_know_sooner
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My wrists know sooner than my temper when I ought to rest. | I open both paws straight out before taking hold of a second heavy thing.
b : What does that do?
a : Gives all those little joints a vote while I'm still disposed to listen. | Stops me carrying the last job's twist into the next one.

scene before_i_pay_for
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I price a length of cloth I look at the space between threads. | Pull the weave across your thumb before you hand over your coin.
b : What do you hope to see between the threads?
a : A gap that opens and closes without leaving a ladder behind. | Enough cloth there that the first wring won't turn my purchase into a net.

scene in_pinching_times_i
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In pinching times I keep my soap heels in a scrap of mesh. | If a new cake of soap's out of reach I still want the old ends together.
b : Why in mesh?
a : Little ends rub a lather up between them and I'm spared chasing scraps round a tub. | They'll do one more job in company than any of them can do alone.

scene don_t_tell_me
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Don't tell me one end of a load weighs the same as the other without lifting it. | A bundle can look tidy while every heavy bit's hiding at one end.
b : How would you set it right?
a : Move one folded thing. Ask both carriers again. They'll let you know. | Balance it on a stool first. Whichever end hits your toe needs lightening.

scene i_like_the_moment
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like the moment a knot holds without another finger on it. | A good bundle should forgive one loose turn.
b : How can you be sure it'll hold?
a : Lift an inch. If the tail slides, put it down while you've still got the choice. | Roll it gently sideways before anybody hoists it. There's your answer.

scene i_can_remember_a
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember a piece of cloth by the shape of its worst patch. | Some repairs are so well done the old hole becomes the strongest place.
b : What does one of those look like?
a : A little oval, stitches close together, no hard ridge to rub through from inside. | More patience on the underside than on the part that shows.

scene rain_s_no_enemy
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain's no enemy to a wolf with everything still soaking in the tub. | A shower always seems to know when something's nearly ready to take in.
b : What do you save first?
a : Whatever took the longest to wring out. My wrists have strong opinions. | Small stuff I could tuck inside my coat. I won't carry the whole sky at once.

scene the_hills_here_teach
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hills here teach me more about a load than a set of scales. | I measure the height of each hill by how often I swap arms.
b : Do you have a favourite landing?
a : One with a ledge high enough that I needn't bend to pick up again. | The last landing before I remember I've something further to carry.

scene a_buttered_oatcake_travels
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A buttered oatcake travels better in good cloth than in a warm bare paw. | I wrap the last bite separately if I'm walking far.
b : Why save one bite?
a : On a long road the last corner tastes as good as the whole first cake. | It feels like a present from the wolf I was when I set out.

scene don_t_offer_me
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Don't offer me pity in the voice you'd use to order me about. | If I snap at an offer it may be the tone that's caught my fur.
b : How should the offer sound?
a : Like a question I'll really be allowed to answer either way. | Talk to me level. I'm easy to help once nobody's trying to arrange me.

scene i_ask_the_bright
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I speak to the Bright One, it's a gentle grip I want more often than a strong back. | I don't need much ceremony to give thanks after I've set down a load.
b : A gentle grip on what?
a : Usually on my temper. Other things can stay held well enough. | Whatever's been handed back to me more tenderly than I expected.

scene i_ll_offer_a
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll offer a newcomer a piece out of my clean bread cloth. | It's easy to help somebody in a way that puts the whole street in on it.
b : What makes a private kindness possible?
a : Make it ordinary. Hand over the cake like I'm passing a pin. | Speak softly and once. There's no need to announce a refusal either.

scene i_don_t_like
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't like walks measured in the number of useful things I do along the way. | Sometimes I go out to see how far I can get without acquiring an errand.
b : What if a friend needs help?
a : Then my walk has become a visit and I can have my walk some other time. | I help if it's needed. Nobody gets to put the walk down in an account.

scene a_damp_rag_by
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp rag by a latch makes a whole room smell like a forgotten job. | I leave a gap around anything drying, even the meanest dishcloth.
b : Does a gap matter so much?
a : Touch two wet folds in the morning and try to tell me air doesn't earn its keep. | I like getting a second use out of one day's airing.

scene i_d_finish_my
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd finish my own bundle before giving an opinion on yours. | When I'm working I count what's come in before I count what's gone out.
b : Doesn't that take twice the time?
a : Less time than searching the town for a cuff that never came through the door. | It takes the heat out of a disagreement when both counts match.

scene i_remember_making_a
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember making a parcel look grander than the thing wrapped up in it. | I've spent more string than sense on a present before now.
b : What were you giving?
a : One plain oatcake to a friend with a long hungry walk ahead. | A square of good cloth. I'd wrapped the wrapper and forgotten to laugh about it.

scene somebody_put_it_about
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody put it about that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I've heard this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Would you put your mark against it?
a : On a clean sheet I'd mark only that I've heard it. Mind the difference. | No. A repeat costs breath. A guarantee would cost my good name.

story button [topic=work]
  : Once a button dropped into a tub and I fished round to the elbow.
  : I came up with two buttons and a strip of very decisive blue ribbon.
  b : Did you find the one you lost?
  : Still on a thread round my wrist. The morning went by trying to account for the other two.

story birds [topic=food]
  : I wrapped an oatcake so neatly that I wrapped an empty cloth the same way for practice.
  : A gull went sailing off with a parcel before I'd stowed the pair.
  b : Did you lose your supper?
  : I had the cake. The gull had a useful lesson which seemed to make it very cross.

story walk [topic=travel]
  : I went out for a walk and took an empty basket for no sensible reason.
  : By the far corner I'd filled it with things I thought I might use at home.
  b : Was the walk worth it?
  : The return half taught me what an empty paw was worth. Next time I took only my coat.

story mark [topic=memories]
  : I once marked the underside of a patch with a tiny row of dots.
  : I folded it twice, set it aside and spent a whole evening looking for my mark.
  b : When did the mark turn up?
  : In my own very clever hiding place. My own discretion had kept me completely in the dark.

story stroke [topic=faith]
  : I tried counting bells while pulling a knot apart with my teeth.
  : The knot came loose on a stroke and my two counts came wonderfully mixed.
  b : Which count did you keep?
  : The knot was open. I called it one and let the chapel keep the rest.

rule @linen
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That edge wants turning towards the middle. | Keep the marked corner out of sight.

rule @wrists
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Straighten the fingers before another twist. | A grip should end when the job does.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A bell's an unkind way to stir a sleeper. | My wrists aren't taking early orders from the sky.

rule @wet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cover the dry things nearest your shoulder. | Keep a corner for wiping your eyes clear.

rule @home
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save a little walking for yourself. | Fine light for a walk with empty arms.

rule @lesson
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Find where the strain is before showing off a grip. | Let the learner feel the balance first.

dlg resident.hub : Mind the bundle if you take the nearer seat.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your hands on your own business and I'll hear you.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, come where we can talk at an ordinary volume.
dlg resident.job [self.job=laborer] : #self.workplace# keeps my wrists busy. Clean cloth has to find its own door again too.
dlg resident.job : I like work where I can give a thing back in better shape.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's the news as it came into my hands. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Allow for a few twists on the way round.
dlg resident.bye : May the next load sit comfortably.
dlg master.work : Get a feel for the weight before you agree to carry it. A trade lives in the fingers as much as the head.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : There's room under my wing for a single learner I trust. Ask and I'll take you on.
dlg master.wages : There's no apprentice wage. You'll learn three times faster beside me, and can sell whatever your hands turn out.
dlg master.bye : Give those fingers a rest on your way.
graft resident.hub
choice Why hide the mark on the cloth? -> corner_privacy
node corner_privacy
say You come to me with a bundle. It comes back. Between those two moments nobody has paid for the right to pick over your affairs.
choice What if you mix them up? -> corner_pair
choice I'll leave it folded. -> hub
node corner_pair
say Two halves of a tally or a quick look inside the fold. A whole street doesn't need to help me read.
choice I see how that works. -> bye
graft master.learn
choice Can I try balancing a bundle? -> corner_balance
node corner_balance
say Start close to the ground. Take the weight against your palm, with the other hand open underneath till you know which way it'll tip.
choice The far corner pulls. -> corner_repack
choice Another day, perhaps. -> learn
node corner_repack
say Set it down before you shift the heavy part. No prize for holding on with your teeth when there's a perfectly good floor.
choice I'll put it down. -> learn
